## ex5 - inferring through a constructor

`infer` is not limited to call signatures. Construct signatures work the same
way, and getting the pattern right matters when you type a factory or a DI
container.

Edit `ex5/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export type Constructed<C> = /* the instance type C builds, or never */;
export type CtorArgs<C> = /* the constructor parameter tuple, or never */;
```

Expected, with

```ts
abstract class Repo { constructor(public url: string, public retries: number) {} }
class Wire { constructor(public id: string) {} }
```

```ts
type _1 = Expect<Equal<Constructed<typeof Repo>, Repo>>;
type _2 = Expect<Equal<CtorArgs<typeof Repo>, [url: string, retries: number]>>;
type _3 = Expect<Equal<Constructed<typeof Wire>, Wire>>;
type _4 = Expect<Equal<Constructed<string>, never>>;
```

Two details the gate is deliberately strict about: `Repo` is `abstract`, and the
expected tuple carries its parameter *labels*. A pattern that loses either one
fails.

